<title>JAPAN: Hohrin shares bid-only in mid-morning.</title>
<headline>Hohrin shares bid-only in mid-morning.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hohrin Co Ltd were bid-only in mid-morning Tuesday trade after Israel's Lorenzi Diamond Ltd said it planned to take a 44 percent stake in the Japanese jewellery importer, brokers said.</p>
<p>Hohrin's shares were bid at 1,100 yen at 0117 GMT in the over-the-counter market. They closed at 1,040 yen on Monday.</p>
<p>Japanese economic daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said the Israeli diamond exporter would buy the shares from the founder and former chairman of Hohrin, Tadahiko Ura, for about 1.91 billion yen.</p>
</text>
